---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import SiteHeader from '../components/SiteHeader.astro';
import SiteFooter from '../components/SiteFooter.astro';
import RandomPokemonGenerator from '../components/RandomPokemonGenerator';
---
<BaseLayout title="Random Pokémon Generator – Pick 1 or a Team of 6" description="Generate random Pokémon with pictures. Filter by generation, type and evolution, lock favorites, reroll and analyze your team. Free, no signup."><SiteHeader/><main id="main" class="random-page"><h1>Random Pokémon Generator</h1><p class="intro">Pick one Pokémon or a random team of six. Free · No signup · No duplicates.</p><RandomPokemonGenerator client:load/><section class="seo-content"><h2>From a random pick to your next team</h2><p>Choose a quantity, optionally filter the pool, and select Generate. Lock any result you want to keep, then generate again to reroll the other slots. Use Copy names for a drawing prompt or a challenge with friends.</p><h2>What does the generator include?</h2><p>The pool contains 1,025 base species, National Pokédex #001–1025, from Bulbasaur to Pecharunt. Regional, Mega and other alternate forms are excluded. Type filters use Generation 9 typing. Each eligible species has an equal chance in an unlocked draw, without duplicate species in the same result. Scores do not influence random selection.</p><h2>Can I generate a random Pokémon team?</h2><p>Yes. Choose six, then lock favorites or reroll individual slots. Analyze this team sends the results into our <a href="/">Pokémon team builder</a> to inspect typing, base stats, <a href="/weakness-calculator">shared weaknesses</a> and <a href="/type-coverage">offensive coverage</a>. Transfer happens in this browser tab; it does not overwrite saved teams.</p><h2>Does a generation filter mean I can catch them in that game?</h2><p>No. It selects the generation in which each species first appeared. It does not check encounters, trading, events, game availability or competitive legality. Random teams are casual starting points, not guaranteed viable teams or a ROM randomizer.</p><h2>How do the extra filters work?</h2><p>Turn off legendary and mythical Pokémon to exclude those categories. Ultra Beasts and Paradox Pokémon remain eligible unless another filter excludes them. Fully evolved also includes species without an evolution; evolution status follows the modern dataset rather than historical games.</p><p>Data: the project's pinned @pkmn/dex dependency. <a href="/about">Data sources and methodology</a>. No live API calls are required for each draw.</p></section></main><SiteFooter/></BaseLayout>
